\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=4 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nThe supplied nullspace can be written as the span of the independent vectors in\n\n$${x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$$\n\nHence $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$, so $A$ is not invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<4$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{4}$. In particular, $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$ is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$.\n\n- Statement $A\\text{ is invertible}$ is false. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4$ is true. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$; $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4$ only." 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673191 1080 "I only" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673191 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673191 1083 #uuid "1522bd23-2fc5-5e8e-81c9-c3ca0adfaab8" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186673221 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186673228 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673192 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673192 1077 "$A\\text{ is invertible}$" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673192 1078 #edb/ref 17592186673221 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673192 1079 #uuid "1ae79cff-5786-59fd-8689-3572a75aa7ee" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673193 1080 "false" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673193 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673193 1083 #uuid "1def3aa4-ca90-5a60-ae81-18f879b8fddb" 13194139538750 1759218604544