$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$ is false. $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$.\n\n- Statement $A\\text{ is not invertible}$ is true. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ is false. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A\\text{ is not invertible}$ only." 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673227 1080 "true" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673227 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673227 1083 #uuid "ce459033-934c-5e8f-9cc5-1373e4c9dc76" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673228 1080 "true" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673228 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673228 1083 #uuid "db683bfe-2cbe-534a-967e-0caacc6a700a" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673229 1075 #edb/ref 17592186673218 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673229 1075 #edb/ref 17592186673227 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673229 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673229 1077 "$\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673229 1078 #edb/ref 17592186673227 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673229 1079 #uuid "dca096b0-234a-53b0-8389-67623d2617b5" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673230 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673195 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673230 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673230 1071 "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)=7$?\n\nI. $A\\text{ is invertible}$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{7}$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673230 1072 #uuid "e41f879e-5e60-5636-a17a-b03256796798" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673230 1074 "Since $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{7} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=7 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nThe given full rank implies that $A$ is invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)=7$, $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$, $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true: $A\\text{ is invertible}$. $A$ is invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false: $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{7}$. $\\text{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$.\n\n- Statement III is true: $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I and III only." 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673231 1080 "true" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673231 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673231 1083 #uuid "e7ce894c-68e9-5937-8695-76780148fcbe" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673232 1080 "I and II only" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673232 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673232 1083 #uuid "e8fcdf25-49f6-5816-a304-cabb301b89ee" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673233 1080 "true" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673233 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673233 1083 #uuid "f14c2be7-6d66-59ed-8e7e-b0e8ed2d34b3" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673234 1080 "I only" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673234 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673234 1083 #uuid "f15e8fed-707c-5062-8e6e-f4b9c86ecce0" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673235 1080 "false" 13194139538750 17592186045443 true] [17592186673235 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538750 17592186045443